    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0262" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.51/993: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Scotten</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-28T10:00:00-06:00">May 28, 1942—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>282. My 279, May 27, 5 p.m. obviously crossed the Department’s No. 207, May 27, 2
                    p.m. I propose therefore if the Department approves <pb facs="0263" n="249"
                        xml:id="pg249"/> to withhold action on the Department’s 207 until the
                    Department has an opportunity to comment on my 279.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Scotten</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
